.TH SPARKY-STEREO-CAMERA 1 "November 2026" "sparky-stereo-camera 0.1.3" "Sparky Stereo OS"
.SH NAME
sparky-stereo-camera \- the Camera page of System Settings, as a command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sparky-stereo-camera
[\fB\-\-no\-save\fR] \fBlist\fR | \fBdefault\fR [\fINAME\fR] | \fBformats\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBbest\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBmode\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIFOURCC WxH FPS\fR] | \fBcontrols\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBcontrol\fR \fINAME CONTROL\fR [\fIVALUE\fR] | \fBreset\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBpacking\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIID\fR|\fBlist\fR] | \fBsave\fR \fINAME\fR | \fBapply\fR [\fINAME\fR] | \fBwatch\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
A camera is named by its PipeWire node name (see \fBlist\fR). \fBdefault\fR reads or sets the session's default video source
(WirePlumber's default.configured.video.source), which every program that asks PipeWire for a camera follows.
\fBmode\fR and \fBcontrol\fR set the camera's format, size, frame rate or one control on the V4L2 device and keep the choice in
~/.config/sparky-stereo-camera/cameras.ini unless \fB\-\-no\-save\fR comes first.
Only a setting is kept: a control with a range (or a menu or a boolean) that the camera takes and reports and that is active;
a read-only, write-only, volatile, relative or speed control, an action, or one without a range is shown by \fBcontrols\fR with its
reason in the field \fBkeep\fR and never saved.
\fBbest\fR prints the mode a camera starts at when no mode is saved for it: its largest picture, and at that size its highest frame
rate, among the formats a known machine's caveat names (sparky-stereo-hardware's table).
\fBapply\fR sets the saved choices again (the controls that change the picture's layout, the saved or the best mode, then the other
controls, a governing control before the one it governs); a saved setting that is inactive is left for when it is active; \fBwatch\fR does so whenever a camera appears, and is what the user service sparky-stereo-camera.service runs.
\fBpacking\fR keeps how a two-lens camera packs its two pictures, by the stereo layer's input list (\fBpacking NAME list\fR prints it).
.PP
Output is JSON. Exit status 0 is success, 1 a failure the command says, 2 a wrong command line, 3 no default camera.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
SPARKY_STEREO_CAMERA_SYSFS
Replaces /sys where a camera's USB ids are read (a test rig's virtual cameras).
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/sparky-stereo-camera/cameras.ini
What the person chose for each camera.
.TP
~/.local/state/wireplumber/default-nodes
Where WirePlumber keeps the default camera.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpw-dump\fR(1), \fBpw-metadata\fR(1), \fBwireplumber\fR(1)
